1
00:00:33,036 --> 00:00:34,067
[This drama is fiction.]

2
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:36,223
[Characters, places, events, organization,
and the setting have no connection to reality.]

3
00:00:36,223 --> 00:00:38,151
[Child actors
were filmed under safe conditions.]

4
00:00:38,151 --> 00:00:40,231
[Episode 3]

5
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:48,285
Get home safe.

6
00:00:48,285 --> 00:00:50,346
- Take care.
- You too.

7
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:55,698
Hye Seong!

8
00:01:15,110 --> 00:01:20,620
Wow! Look at you! Looking pretty good in Seoul.

9
00:01:22,470 --> 00:01:24,976
And you got a job at such a fancy firm.

10
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:28,249
Why haven't you stayed in touch?

11
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:35,913
What's wrong?

12
00:01:37,209 --> 00:01:39,766
Hey! What are you doing?

13
00:01:44,170 --> 00:01:46,315
What's wrong with you?

14
00:01:46,315 --> 00:01:48,288
Seriously.

15
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:16,487
<i>How can you be so rude to your mother?</i>

16
00:02:16,487 --> 00:02:18,591
<i>And where's my 300 million won?</i>

17
00:02:18,591 --> 00:02:22,210
<i>My share of the assets for raising you.</i>

18
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:24,215
<i>You stopped being my mother long ago.</i>

19
00:02:24,215 --> 00:02:26,597
<i>So don't ever come here again!</i>

20
00:02:26,597 --> 00:02:29,083
<i>Don't show up in front of Dad either.</i>

21
00:02:29,083 --> 00:02:31,317
<i>Does that mean I'm not your mother?</i>

22
00:02:31,317 --> 00:02:33,737
<i>Don't you know you can't legally
sever family ties?</i>

23
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:18,620
<i>Hey! What are you doing?</i>

24
00:03:25,265 --> 00:03:29,635
[Attorney Kang, did you get home safe?]

25
00:03:34,290 --> 00:03:37,040
<i>Yes, ma'am. See you next week.</i>

26
00:03:46,653 --> 00:03:47,829
[REBOM Secretary Kim]

27
00:03:58,590 --> 00:04:02,510
Fried eggs are all I'll let you handle.
It's dangerous.

28
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:04,730
- I'm almost an adult now.
- Oh, please.

29
00:04:04,730 --> 00:04:07,080
Ji Yoon cooks a lot when we go camping.

30
00:04:07,715 --> 00:04:11,115
Ji Yoon? What does she cook?

31
00:04:11,115 --> 00:04:12,790
She invents new ramyeon recipes.

32
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:17,240
She mixes two or three kinds of ramyeon
into new dishes, and they're really good.

33
00:04:20,470 --> 00:04:25,190
Kim Jae Hee, you smile a lot
whenever you talk about Ji Yoon.

34
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:30,970
You said being family felt awkward.
Are you all used to it now?

35
00:04:30,970 --> 00:04:32,520
Yeah, for sure.

36
00:04:37,350 --> 00:04:39,250
- The yolk broke!
- I know!

37
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:41,749
- Flip it, flip it! Quick!
- Flip it?

38
00:04:43,190 --> 00:04:45,110
- Dad!
- Yeah?

39
00:04:45,110 --> 00:04:47,244
This is the last of the boxes.

40
00:04:49,411 --> 00:04:52,390
Moving is so much easier
when they handle everything.

41
00:04:52,390 --> 00:04:54,331
I know.

42
00:04:54,331 --> 00:04:56,545
This is great.

43
00:04:56,545 --> 00:05:00,091
[Ajeongdang Moving]
We used to do all the legwork. Look at this.

44
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:04,430
[All the benefits you have missed, at once!]
It handles every service you need in one go.

45
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:07,440
It's perfect for someone who plans well.
Like you, Dad.

46
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:13,680
- No, I'll carry it.
- I'm fine, really.

47
00:05:15,010 --> 00:05:18,290
- You worked so hard today, Dad.
- You too.

48
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:21,660
- Moving day ends with jjajangmyeon, right?
- Of course.

49
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:26,100
- Let's give our best in Seoul, Hye Seong.
- Yeah, Dad.

50
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:29,878
Thank you.

51
00:05:29,878 --> 00:05:32,047
Thank you for your hard work.

52
00:05:52,870 --> 00:05:54,900
It's so bright.

53
00:05:57,270 --> 00:06:00,030
Wow, my daughter looks so pretty.

54
00:06:00,030 --> 00:06:03,678
I'm a lawyer in Seoul now.
I'll start fresh and do my best.

55
00:06:03,678 --> 00:06:08,798
I'll make sure you
and Attorney Cha never regret trusting me.

56
00:06:08,798 --> 00:06:11,492
I came to Seoul to open a restaurant
and make it big.

57
00:06:11,492 --> 00:06:13,738
Dad, just take it easy now.

58
00:06:13,738 --> 00:06:15,077
I don't want to.

59
00:06:15,077 --> 00:06:18,396
You got this house with an overdraft loan.
How can I just sit back?

60
00:06:18,396 --> 00:06:23,125
I'll learn the know-how for famous tteokbokki
in Seoul, and you learn the know-how at REBOM.

61
00:06:23,125 --> 00:06:25,343
Let's give it our all. Got it?

62
00:06:25,343 --> 00:06:27,140
- Yeah.
- Drink up.

63
00:06:29,681 --> 00:06:35,280
[Case 03: Know-How]

64
00:06:44,518 --> 00:06:45,858
Secretary Kim?

65
00:06:45,858 --> 00:06:49,602
Since it's your first day,
Ma'am ordered me to pick you up personally.

66
00:06:57,964 --> 00:06:59,422
Thank you.

67
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:12,469
[Gossip Sheet Shared]

68
00:07:12,469 --> 00:07:14,893
[1M Economy Creator Lee Jun Sik]
[Affair]

69
00:07:14,893 --> 00:07:16,538
[Devoted Husband Image]
[Divorce Suit]

70
00:07:20,697 --> 00:07:22,670
[Lee Jun Sik's Affair]

71
00:07:22,670 --> 00:07:24,293
[Affair Rumors Ignite Around Lee Jun Sik,
Husband of Lee Young Mi]

72
00:07:24,293 --> 00:07:25,559
[Late-Night Pool Date Spotted]

73
00:07:25,559 --> 00:07:27,385
[Hotel Sightings with a Mystery Woman,
Not His Wife, Spread Like Wildfire]

74
00:07:28,529 --> 00:07:29,959
An affair?

75
00:07:29,959 --> 00:07:31,759
[Lee Jun Sik]

76
00:07:31,759 --> 00:07:32,939
[Lee Jun Sik's Economy TV]

77
00:07:32,939 --> 00:07:35,326
[What If Couples Stop Talking?]
[Couples in Their 50s: Are We Still Steamy?]

78
00:07:35,326 --> 00:07:38,524
I thought they were a devoted couple.

79
00:07:38,524 --> 00:07:41,298
<i>You'll learn all about divorce cases at REBOM.</i>

80
00:07:43,685 --> 00:07:47,048
Don't tell me they're coming to REBOM.

81
00:07:48,264 --> 00:07:50,686
Yes, this is Park Tae Su from By the Law.

82
00:07:50,686 --> 00:07:51,723
[By the Law]

83
00:07:51,723 --> 00:07:53,981
Court compensation is about 20 million won.

84
00:07:53,981 --> 00:07:57,848
It's too little to punish those who cheat.

85
00:08:00,338 --> 00:08:02,826
No, that won't do.

86
00:08:02,826 --> 00:08:07,026
If I belittle people who have affairs,
I'll lose half of my clients.

87
00:08:07,779 --> 00:08:09,408
That's not it.

88
00:08:10,478 --> 00:08:12,177
Good job, everyone.

89
00:08:12,177 --> 00:08:15,626
Why is the subscriber count stuck at 200,000?

90
00:08:16,265 --> 00:08:17,664
Should I try changing the concept?

91
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:19,183
Sir.

92
00:08:19,183 --> 00:08:21,938
That's a lot. You're at the top among lawyers.

93
00:08:21,938 --> 00:08:24,504
If I'm doing this, I'm going for a million.

94
00:08:26,449 --> 00:08:32,338
Speaking of which, how about content
where we interview actual clients?

95
00:08:32,338 --> 00:08:34,918
Good idea!
The person coming in later would be perfect.

96
00:08:34,918 --> 00:08:36,888
Exactly. That's what I'm saying.

97
00:08:37,547 --> 00:08:43,118
If I feature the one everyone's talking about,
the algorithm will double my subscribers!

98
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:45,141
That's a winning angle.

99
00:08:55,185 --> 00:08:56,647
[Doha News Reporter: Attorney Cha Eun Kyung,
please call me when you see this!]

100
00:08:56,647 --> 00:08:58,091
[Mora Media Reporter: Rumors say Lee Jun Sik
and Lee Young Mi are splitting. Is it true?]

101
00:08:58,091 --> 00:08:59,745
[Gyujeong Daily Reporter: Attorney Cha,
are you taking Lee Jun Sik's divorce suit?]

102
00:08:59,745 --> 00:09:01,359
[Saerom Daily Reporter: Are you taking the case
of Lee Jun Sik and Lee Young Mi?]

103
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,312
[Jeongseok News Reporter Kim Tae Jeong]

104
00:09:05,312 --> 00:09:09,759
<i>Hello, Attorney. Could I interview you
about the Lee Jun Sik and Lee Young Mi case?</i>

105
00:09:24,031 --> 00:09:26,072
Attorney Kang Hye Seong?

106
00:09:27,329 --> 00:09:30,703
Attorney Kang!
Do you know how long I have been waiting...

107
00:09:30,703 --> 00:09:33,198
Anyway, congratulations on your first day.

108
00:09:34,382 --> 00:09:35,975
Let me introduce myself.

109
00:09:35,975 --> 00:09:41,118
I'm not a weirdo. I'm Attorney Jeon Eun Ho,
and I work in the office next door.

110
00:09:42,418 --> 00:09:44,124
Hello.

111
00:09:45,077 --> 00:09:47,251
I'm from the courthouse back then...

112
00:09:50,096 --> 00:09:52,299
It's okay.

113
00:09:52,299 --> 00:09:54,828
Did you happen to see the gossip sheet?

114
00:09:55,472 --> 00:09:58,218
Lee Young Mi is coming
in for a consultation today.

115
00:09:58,218 --> 00:10:01,322
- Lee Jun Sik's wife?
- Yes.

116
00:10:01,322 --> 00:10:06,518
Big affair cases reach REBOM
before they hit the news.

117
00:10:06,518 --> 00:10:10,928
Think of us as the front line
of the affair and divorce world.

118
00:10:10,928 --> 00:10:12,706
You came to the right place.

119
00:10:12,706 --> 00:10:14,714
Welcome to REBOM!

120
00:10:21,385 --> 00:10:22,709
Yes.

121
00:10:26,627 --> 00:10:28,726
Hello, Attorney.

122
00:10:30,038 --> 00:10:36,588
Thank you for sending the car,
but I have my own, so I'll be fine from now on.

123
00:10:37,458 --> 00:10:42,488
<i>Ma'am, I think Attorney Park is using
the company car for dates on weekends.</i>

124
00:10:43,598 --> 00:10:45,019
Is that so?

125
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:47,718
That was a first-day perk.

126
00:10:47,718 --> 00:10:50,745
Attorney Kang,
you don't need to greet me every morning.

127
00:10:50,745 --> 00:10:53,086
Save your energy for the cases.

128
00:10:53,086 --> 00:10:57,107
<i>Greeting the boss is the most
basic thing an employee should do!</i>

129
00:11:00,434 --> 00:11:03,334
Attorney, what should I start with?

130
00:11:04,248 --> 00:11:06,460
Join me for the morning consultation.

131
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:07,466
Pardon?

132
00:11:08,586 --> 00:11:10,868
The morning consultation...

133
00:11:12,478 --> 00:11:14,338
With Lee Young Mi?

134
00:11:14,338 --> 00:11:16,238
Yes, that's the one.

135
00:11:16,238 --> 00:11:19,057
I'll read up on the articles and see you then.

136
00:11:32,622 --> 00:11:36,612
[Your Strongest Sword and Shield]

137
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:41,819
[Central Family Court]

138
00:12:02,238 --> 00:12:05,938
It's hibiscus. It's my favorite tea.

139
00:12:05,938 --> 00:12:09,578
I saw you drinking it on the channel,
so I had it prepared.

140
00:12:09,578 --> 00:12:11,028
Thank you.

141
00:12:15,168 --> 00:12:17,674
Shall we get into your case?

142
00:12:19,739 --> 00:12:22,932
How did you find out
about your husband's affair?

143
00:12:23,767 --> 00:12:28,940
I got a message while he was away
on a business trip.

144
00:12:43,928 --> 00:12:47,967
<i>It seems Lee Jun Sik doesn't only
do his Bedroom Talk at home.</i>

145
00:13:03,328 --> 00:13:05,798
<i>- You're Lee Young Mi, right?
- Yes.</i>

146
00:13:06,568 --> 00:13:08,351
<i>Could you sign here?</i>

147
00:13:10,548 --> 00:13:12,638
<i>- Goodbye.
- Thank you.</i>

148
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,977
[Central Family Court]

149
00:13:19,977 --> 00:13:21,651
[Special Delivery]
[To Lee Young Mi]

150
00:13:26,902 --> 00:13:28,481
[Complaint]

151
00:13:28,481 --> 00:13:29,869
[Prayer for relief]

152
00:13:29,869 --> 00:13:31,758
[The plaintiff and defendant shall be divorced]

153
00:13:39,134 --> 00:13:41,318
What are your assets worth?

154
00:13:42,091 --> 00:13:44,358
A bit over 10 billion won in his name.

155
00:13:45,648 --> 00:13:47,378
There's nothing in my name.

156
00:13:50,254 --> 00:13:52,024
What do I do now?

157
00:13:55,268 --> 00:13:58,848
You're the wife of Lee Jun Sik,
a famous creator known nationwide.

158
00:13:58,848 --> 00:14:01,848
How can you have nothing in your name?

159
00:14:01,848 --> 00:14:03,678
That's terrible.

160
00:14:04,703 --> 00:14:08,712
What else? You should divorce him
and divide your assets immediately.

161
00:14:08,712 --> 00:14:11,702
- For whose benefit?
- For yours, of course, Ms. Lee.

162
00:14:11,702 --> 00:14:15,418
Exactly half, five billion won.
I'll get that for you.

163
00:14:17,854 --> 00:14:20,324
How much did you get for living expenses?

164
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:24,156
One and a half million won.

165
00:14:24,156 --> 00:14:25,640
One and a half...

166
00:14:29,868 --> 00:14:33,914
If you don't get a divorce right now,
all that money will go to the mistress.

167
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:37,801
If you look at the bank accounts of men
who are stingy with their wives,

168
00:14:37,801 --> 00:14:40,472
they're usually very generous
with their mistresses.

169
00:14:40,472 --> 00:14:43,402
Sign the contract now and file
for property seizure.

170
00:14:48,523 --> 00:14:52,776
This is my fifth lawyer consultation,
and I still have one more.

171
00:14:52,776 --> 00:14:54,823
I'll decide after I see them.

172
00:15:00,341 --> 00:15:02,177
I'll be going now.

173
00:15:10,628 --> 00:15:12,947
I guess it's because she's rich.

174
00:15:12,947 --> 00:15:16,009
She must go to a lot of lawyer consultations.

175
00:15:16,009 --> 00:15:17,967
That must cost a fortune.

176
00:15:17,967 --> 00:15:22,037
It's not because she's rich.
She's lawyer shopping because she has no money.

177
00:15:22,695 --> 00:15:25,397
She wants someone
who can get her the most money.

178
00:15:25,397 --> 00:15:26,978
She has no money?

179
00:15:26,978 --> 00:15:30,015
She's decked out in luxury brands.

180
00:15:30,015 --> 00:15:33,725
Luxury brands and 10 billion won are useless
if it's all her husband's.

181
00:15:33,725 --> 00:15:36,614
In reality,
she only gets 1.5 million won to live on.

182
00:15:36,614 --> 00:15:40,349
She has no cash,
so she's even taking the free tea with her.

183
00:15:46,054 --> 00:15:49,919
- Let's waive the retainer. Success fee only.
- What?

184
00:15:50,748 --> 00:15:54,628
What if she doesn't divorce?
We won't even get a success fee, sir.

185
00:15:54,628 --> 00:15:55,989
That won't happen.

186
00:15:55,989 --> 00:15:58,689
Money drives most human decisions.

187
00:15:58,689 --> 00:16:01,688
Taking a case and getting a divorce
both come down to money.

188
00:16:01,688 --> 00:16:03,679
If we waive the retainer, she'll sign.

189
00:16:03,679 --> 00:16:06,752
And she'll end up divorcing
over the property split.

190
00:16:09,375 --> 00:16:10,724
Just watch.

191
00:16:15,108 --> 00:16:16,268
This way.

192
00:16:17,186 --> 00:16:19,182
- Hello.
- Welcome.

193
00:16:20,513 --> 00:16:21,815
[By the Law]

194
00:16:23,921 --> 00:16:26,115
I'm Senior Partner Cha Eun Kyung.

195
00:16:28,316 --> 00:16:30,198
- Please, have a seat.
- Okay.

196
00:16:34,582 --> 00:16:37,228
Don't you have hibiscus tea here?

197
00:16:37,228 --> 00:16:39,179
Should I go out and buy some?

198
00:16:39,179 --> 00:16:40,968
Manager Shim?

199
00:16:40,968 --> 00:16:44,713
Please get her some water.

200
00:16:44,713 --> 00:16:46,199
Yes, ma'am.

201
00:16:53,639 --> 00:16:54,688
[Central Family Court]

202
00:17:01,484 --> 00:17:04,248
Hello. I'm Attorney Kang Hye Seong.

203
00:17:04,248 --> 00:17:06,567
Hello.

204
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:09,198
I'm the wife of creator Lee Jun Sik.

205
00:17:11,443 --> 00:17:16,128
How did Lee Jun Sik first start as a creator?

206
00:17:16,128 --> 00:17:17,483
My husband?

207
00:17:18,708 --> 00:17:20,445
Why do you ask?

208
00:17:21,948 --> 00:17:25,683
It matters for the property division
and for your contribution.

209
00:17:26,787 --> 00:17:29,203
Everyone is so focused on the money.

210
00:17:30,608 --> 00:17:34,112
I built that man, and that channel, myself.

211
00:17:34,112 --> 00:17:36,532
[Five years ago]
<i>Honestly. Honey!</i>

212
00:17:36,532 --> 00:17:42,589
Five years ago, my husband was fired from
a big company after 20 years and fell apart.

213
00:17:42,589 --> 00:17:47,285
<i>It's over. I can't get another job at my age.</i>

214
00:17:47,285 --> 00:17:50,841
<i>It's not over. This is just the beginning.</i>

215
00:17:50,841 --> 00:17:55,176
<i>That financial knowledge
of 20 years doesn't just disappear.</i>

216
00:17:55,836 --> 00:17:58,330
<i>Let's start an economy channel.</i>

217
00:17:59,246 --> 00:18:01,692
<i>Who would watch me do something like that?</i>

218
00:18:02,789 --> 00:18:05,071
<i>Get up. Let's go wash your face. Okay?</i>

219
00:18:05,071 --> 00:18:08,323
He started his channel at my suggestion.

220
00:18:08,323 --> 00:18:09,548
<i>Good luck!</i>

221
00:18:09,548 --> 00:18:10,816
<i>Let's do this!</i>

222
00:18:12,148 --> 00:18:14,620
<i>Hello. This is Lee Jun Sik's Economy TV.</i>

223
00:18:17,688 --> 00:18:20,258
<i>Hello. This is Lee Jun Sik's Economy TV.</i>

224
00:18:22,208 --> 00:18:24,038
<i>My views just aren't increasing.</i>

225
00:18:24,646 --> 00:18:26,779
<i>Why don't you try changing the concept?</i>

226
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:33,138
<i>Forget the information and tell your own story.
Like, for example...</i>

227
00:18:34,128 --> 00:18:37,749
<i>"How I quit my big corporate job
and started an economy channel."</i>

228
00:18:39,715 --> 00:18:45,482
<i>Hey followers! Lee Jun Sik's Economy TV
has finally reached 100,000!</i>

229
00:18:45,482 --> 00:18:46,982
<i>The Silver Button!</i>

230
00:18:46,982 --> 00:18:49,582
<i>It's all thanks to you. Thank you.</i>

231
00:18:49,582 --> 00:18:53,686
<i>Mrs. Lee has arrived.
You all know her, right? My wife.</i>

232
00:18:53,686 --> 00:18:55,134
<i>- I...
- Say hello.</i>

233
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,601
<i>Hello.</i>

234
00:18:56,601 --> 00:18:59,798
<i>My wife, she's the goddess behind my success.</i>

235
00:19:03,939 --> 00:19:05,473
[You two have great chemistry!]
[Do a couple's talk to celebrate!]

236
00:19:05,473 --> 00:19:06,828
[Do a couple's story next!]
[Please film content with your wife!]

237
00:19:06,828 --> 00:19:10,595
<i>Okay. A promise is a promise, so I'll keep it.</i>

238
00:19:10,595 --> 00:19:13,160
<i>Until next time, bye, bye!</i>

239
00:19:14,408 --> 00:19:17,938
<i>- You did great, honey.
